      "writtenOn": "2023-07-07T00:33:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems backwards- but not forwards-compatible. Should we do what some of the other handlers do if the length doesn\u0027t match: call `dev_err` and then return? Alternatively, what `_handle_release` does: only return if we didn\u0027t get enough bytes?",
